WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:01.920
So here in our show,

2
00:00:01.920 --> 00:00:04.700
we really love trying to make good things happen

3
00:00:04.700 --> 00:00:06.900
for people that we have on the show.

4
00:00:06.900 --> 00:00:08.950
And when the cameras stop rolling,

5
00:00:08.950 --> 00:00:10.060
the story isn't over.

6
00:00:10.060 --> 00:00:13.130
I'm constantly wondering how they've been doing

7
00:00:13.130 --> 00:00:14.610
after we've said goodbye.

8
00:00:14.610 --> 00:00:18.210
And I really mean it when I say let's keep in touch.

9
00:00:18.210 --> 00:00:22.100
So I invited a few of our inspiring guests back today

10
00:00:22.100 --> 00:00:24.020
for a little check-in.

11
00:00:24.020 --> 00:00:24.970
But first,

12
00:00:24.970 --> 00:00:27.010
why don't we have a little refresh

13
00:00:27.010 --> 00:00:29.690
on when they were on the show and what their stories are.

14
00:00:29.690 --> 00:00:30.792
Take a look.

15
00:00:30.792 --> 00:00:33.640
(gentle music)

16
00:00:33.640 --> 00:00:37.180
I love this next story about a dad

17
00:00:37.180 --> 00:00:40.750
who built a no-judgment food pantry on his lawn

18
00:00:40.750 --> 00:00:43.250
for anyone who needed groceries.

19
00:00:43.250 --> 00:00:45.740
And when donations started pouring in,

20
00:00:45.740 --> 00:00:49.920
he had to turn his entire garage into a safe place

21
00:00:49.920 --> 00:00:51.790
for a community in need.

22
00:00:51.790 --> 00:00:54.130
I'd love a bigger space and just help out more people.

23
00:00:54.130 --> 00:00:56.860
Our friends at Conagra Brand believe

24
00:00:56.860 --> 00:01:00.370 line:15%
that everyone should have access to great and healthy food.

25
00:01:00.370 --> 00:01:02.560
This is from Conagra to you.

26
00:01:02.560 --> 00:01:04.755
Thank you so much, (indistinct).

27
00:01:04.755 --> 00:01:06.075
Thank you, Barney.

28
00:01:06.075 --> 00:01:06.908
Oh my God.

29
00:01:06.908 --> 00:01:09.570 line:15%
11 year old, Zach Hartman has made it his mission

30
00:01:09.570 --> 00:01:10.900 line:15%
to give back to those in need

31
00:01:10.900 --> 00:01:15.140
by finding new homes for used books and stuffed animals.

32
00:01:15.140 --> 00:01:18.390
I collected and donated over 65,000 books.

33
00:01:18.390 --> 00:01:22.010
You needed like an extra at $1,900 to reach your goal.

34
00:01:22.010 --> 00:01:23.410
We wanna give you that money.

35
00:01:23.410 --> 00:01:25.675
And do you know what, I'm just gonna do 5,000.

36
00:01:25.675 --> 00:01:26.950
Thank you.

37
00:01:26.950 --> 00:01:29.073
Say hello to Alejandro Diasgranados

38
00:01:31.095 --> 00:01:33.520
from Aiton Elementary School.

39
00:01:33.520 --> 00:01:35.110
My personal mission always has been

40
00:01:35.110 --> 00:01:38.020 line:15%
to give my students access to a variety of people,

41
00:01:38.020 --> 00:01:40.480 line:15%
programs, resources, and connections to

42
00:01:40.480 --> 00:01:42.470 line:15%
and really enhance their learning experience.

43
00:01:42.470 --> 00:01:45.890
We actually reached out to Asus

44
00:01:45.890 --> 00:01:49.320
and they are giving us enough Asus Chromebooks

45
00:01:49.320 --> 00:01:53.043
for every single student and teacher at Aiton Elementary.

46
00:01:55.944 --> 00:01:58.430
I can't even fathom this.

47
00:01:58.430 --> 00:01:59.290
This is crazy.

48
00:01:59.290 --> 00:02:01.480
He saw a burning car on the street

49
00:02:01.480 --> 00:02:04.560
with a mother and her three children inside.

50
00:02:04.560 --> 00:02:07.920
He risked his own life to pull each one of them out.

51
00:02:07.920 --> 00:02:11.440
The mayor wanted to give you this proclamation,

52
00:02:11.440 --> 00:02:14.260 line:15%
and that's not all, it's Carmelo Anthony.

53
00:02:14.260 --> 00:02:15.093 line:15%
What?

54
00:02:15.093 --> 00:02:16.580
I want to let you know how inspiring

55
00:02:16.580 --> 00:02:17.900
and courageous you are, man.

56
00:02:17.900 --> 00:02:19.440
You are true, true hero.

57
00:02:19.440 --> 00:02:22.490
So we're gonna hook you on some joint brands march

58
00:02:22.490 --> 00:02:23.706
as small thank you--
No way.

59
00:02:23.706 --> 00:02:25.890
For the big thing that've been doing, man.

60
00:02:25.890 --> 00:02:28.600
We also found out that you're a fan of the Brooklyn Nets.

61
00:02:28.600 --> 00:02:30.370
So we have hooked you all up.

62
00:02:30.370 --> 00:02:32.020
We're getting you season passes.

63
00:02:32.020 --> 00:02:34.200
The players are excited to meet you.

64
00:02:34.200 --> 00:02:35.820
Thank you, Justin.
Thank you so much.

65
00:02:35.820 --> 00:02:37.460
Thank you, Justin.

66
00:02:37.460 --> 00:02:38.940
Hello, Monique.

67
00:02:38.940 --> 00:02:41.630 line:15%
You founded a non-profit dance studio,

68
00:02:41.630 --> 00:02:43.267 line:15%
serving underprivileged kids.

69
00:02:43.267 --> 00:02:45.800
When I was coming up, we didn't have the extra funds.

70
00:02:45.800 --> 00:02:48.110
So I wanted to make sure that I can offer that

71
00:02:48.110 --> 00:02:50.600
to every youth that I came in contact with.

72
00:02:50.600 --> 00:02:52.200
I just wanna say thank you.

73
00:02:52.200 --> 00:02:55.547
And I'd also like to contribute $10,000.

74
00:02:55.547 --> 00:02:57.627
Oh my God.

75
00:02:57.627 --> 00:02:59.573
Get outta here, Drew.

76
00:02:59.573 --> 00:03:01.640
Don't make me cry on TV, Drew.

77
00:03:01.640 --> 00:03:02.580
Don't do that.

78
00:03:05.194 --> 00:03:08.361
(audience applauding)

79
00:03:09.290 --> 00:03:11.640
Okay, return I'm like.

80
00:03:11.640 --> 00:03:14.540
Returning to the show are a Barney, Zach,

81
00:03:14.540 --> 00:03:17.310
Justin, Alejandro and Monique.

82
00:03:17.310 --> 00:03:18.230
Hi, guys.

83
00:03:18.230 --> 00:03:19.063
Welcome back.

84
00:03:20.656 --> 00:03:22.850
Hello.

85
00:03:22.850 --> 00:03:23.953
Barney.

86
00:03:24.880 --> 00:03:25.930
Drew.

87
00:03:25.930 --> 00:03:27.070
How are you?

88
00:03:27.070 --> 00:03:30.923
How is the food pantry going since we last spoke?

89
00:03:32.030 --> 00:03:33.380
So I'm great.

90
00:03:33.380 --> 00:03:34.440
Thank you again, by the way,

91
00:03:34.440 --> 00:03:37.410 line:15%
being on your first show, that was such an honor.

92
00:03:37.410 --> 00:03:39.450 line:15%
I'm still getting our Amazon packages today

93
00:03:39.450 --> 00:03:41.400 line:15%
from people who saw me on your show.

94
00:03:41.400 --> 00:03:42.430 line:15%
So thank you.

95
00:03:42.430 --> 00:03:43.263 line:15%
Yes, it's awesome.

96
00:03:43.263 --> 00:03:44.403 line:15%
Thank you so much.

97
00:03:45.470 --> 00:03:49.010
I mean we're every other week still we're about 150

98
00:03:49.010 --> 00:03:50.530
to 175 people.

99
00:03:50.530 --> 00:03:52.430
We were up to 300 at one point,

100
00:03:52.430 --> 00:03:55.820
which was mind-blowing and so awesome.

101
00:03:55.820 --> 00:03:58.720
I mean, we're trucking along and trying to grow this thing

102
00:03:58.720 --> 00:04:00.000
and help as many people as possible.

103
00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:01.080
And you are a huge part of that.

104
00:04:01.080 --> 00:04:02.429
So thank you.

105
00:04:02.429 --> 00:04:05.080
That makes me so happy.

106
00:04:05.080 --> 00:04:08.970
And my beautiful friend, Zach and his mom.

107
00:04:08.970 --> 00:04:09.863
Hi, guys.

108
00:04:10.757 --> 00:04:11.590
Hey.

109
00:04:11.590 --> 00:04:12.540
Hi.

110
00:04:12.540 --> 00:04:14.380
How's everything going?

111
00:04:14.380 --> 00:04:15.440
We're really busy.

112
00:04:15.440 --> 00:04:18.990 line:15%
So I was able to order 50 Zach's packs

113
00:04:18.990 --> 00:04:23.200 line:15%
and 500 books with the money that you've donated to us.

114
00:04:23.200 --> 00:04:25.810
And I've also donated 2000 books

115
00:04:25.810 --> 00:04:28.320
to a local title one school.

116
00:04:28.320 --> 00:04:31.110
Also I've upcycled 200 stuffed animals,

117
00:04:31.110 --> 00:04:32.460
and I've given them to a--

118
00:04:32.460 --> 00:04:33.293
Humane society.

119
00:04:33.293 --> 00:04:35.020
A humane society in Louisiana

120
00:04:35.020 --> 00:04:38.110
that got hit by one of our most recent hurricanes.

121
00:04:38.110 --> 00:04:40.110
So I've been really busy.

122
00:04:40.110 --> 00:04:41.620
Thank you, Zach and Kim.

123
00:04:41.620 --> 00:04:42.813
Thank you truly.

124
00:04:44.270 --> 00:04:46.192
Justin.

125
00:04:46.192 --> 00:04:47.520
Hi.

126
00:04:47.520 --> 00:04:51.063
I cannot stop thinking about your smile.

127
00:04:51.920 --> 00:04:53.780
How are you?

128
00:04:53.780 --> 00:04:55.650
School was going great for me.

129
00:04:55.650 --> 00:04:58.190 line:15%
I should be getting my high school diploma by September.

130
00:04:58.190 --> 00:05:00.693 line:15%
Is it your GED, what is the program?

131
00:05:01.620 --> 00:05:03.552 line:15%
I actually re-enrolled at the school.

132
00:05:03.552 --> 00:05:04.491
Really?

133
00:05:04.491 --> 00:05:05.324
Justin!

134
00:05:08.912 --> 00:05:11.912
Oh, Justin you're just the greatest.

135
00:05:12.867 --> 00:05:17.150
Now I also wanna check in with our friend, Alejandro,

136
00:05:17.150 --> 00:05:18.107
how are you?

137
00:05:19.099 --> 00:05:21.184
I am doing well.

138
00:05:21.184 --> 00:05:24.000
You know, things have been really exciting since the show,

139
00:05:24.000 --> 00:05:26.410
both current and former students reached out.

140
00:05:26.410 --> 00:05:29.350 line:15%
So many families really wanted me

141
00:05:29.350 --> 00:05:32.760 line:15%
to give their deepest thank you for this gift.

142
00:05:32.760 --> 00:05:34.700
And one more cool thing that actually happened

143
00:05:34.700 --> 00:05:37.540
since the show, so that same week,

144
00:05:37.540 --> 00:05:41.410
I was actually surprised with an announcement

145
00:05:41.410 --> 00:05:45.330
that I was named the 2021 DC teacher of the year,

146
00:05:45.330 --> 00:05:46.543
which was exciting.

147
00:05:46.543 --> 00:05:48.755
(audience applauding)

148
00:05:48.755 --> 00:05:49.588
Yay!

149
00:05:52.974 --> 00:05:53.974
I love that.

150
00:05:54.843 --> 00:05:57.130
Thank you so, so much for this.

151
00:05:57.130 --> 00:05:59.070
Well, congratulations, Alejandro.

152
00:05:59.070 --> 00:06:01.340
So well deserved and I'll see you soon.

153
00:06:01.340 --> 00:06:03.094
See you soon, Drew.

154
00:06:03.094 --> 00:06:04.400
Thank you.

155
00:06:04.400 --> 00:06:08.510
And last but not least welcome back, Monique.

156
00:06:08.510 --> 00:06:10.800
I feel like I just saw you the other day.

157
00:06:10.800 --> 00:06:14.410
How's everything going for you and your students?

158
00:06:14.410 --> 00:06:16.300
Oh my God, so much has happened.

159
00:06:16.300 --> 00:06:19.300 line:15%
So let me start by saying a lot of people were touched

160
00:06:19.300 --> 00:06:23.880 line:15%
by the episode that we did and we received donations.

161
00:06:23.880 --> 00:06:27.270
We had multiple families reaching out to us,

162
00:06:27.270 --> 00:06:30.830
wanting to sign their kids up for the organization.

163
00:06:30.830 --> 00:06:35.010
Most recently we had the Daytona International Speedway

164
00:06:35.010 --> 00:06:37.920
contact us and asks us if we could perform

165
00:06:37.920 --> 00:06:39.680
during their race week

166
00:06:39.680 --> 00:06:41.920
where the students will be performing in front

167
00:06:41.920 --> 00:06:44.213
of over 100,000 people.

168
00:06:45.708 --> 00:06:48.190
So much has happened.

169
00:06:48.190 --> 00:06:49.423
So many good things.

170
00:06:50.347 --> 00:06:54.450
I'm so glad that we are linked in the chain of your story

171
00:06:54.450 --> 00:06:57.050
and you deserve all of this.

172
00:06:57.050 --> 00:06:58.660
And I am so happy.

173
00:06:58.660 --> 00:07:01.740
I love when a little spark ignites a fire.

174
00:07:01.740 --> 00:07:03.060
That's perfect,

175
00:07:03.060 --> 00:07:05.500
but you're the one who built the whole thing.

176
00:07:05.500 --> 00:07:07.270
Thank you so much, Drew.

177
00:07:07.270 --> 00:07:09.430
No, Monique, thank you.

178
00:07:09.430 --> 00:07:10.974
You are so awesome.

179
00:07:10.974 --> 00:07:12.900
This is the best news in the world.

180
00:07:12.900 --> 00:07:15.110
Thank you, thank you.

181
00:07:15.110 --> 00:07:18.023
Barney, Zach, Justin, Alejandro and Monique,

182
00:07:19.734 --> 00:07:21.160
thank you for the check-in.

183
00:07:21.160 --> 00:07:22.491
We'll talk to you soon.

184
00:07:22.491 --> 00:07:25.074 line:15%
(upbeat music)

